---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ContactButton from '../components/ContactButton.astro';
import { ASSAY_RUNS, ASSAY_SOURCE, byTool, SCORING_LIVE } from '../lib/benchmark';
import '../styles/landing.css';
const rows = byTool(ASSAY_RUNS);
---
<BaseLayout landing title="Verify AI-authored fixes" description="Assay checks AI-written SQL injection fixes against attacks and normal inputs. Explore the benchmark, inspect the evidence, or talk to our team." path="/">
  <Hero />

  <section class="landing-section shell" aria-labelledby="hinge-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Why independent</p>
    <h2 id="hinge-title">The one thing a fixer can never sell you.</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">An author cannot grade their own work. Every AI fixer today does exactly that, checking its patch against the scanner it was written to satisfy. Assay is the independent party, and that is not a feature anyone can add: it is about who does the looking.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-section shell" id="results" aria-labelledby="results-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The evidence</p><h2 id="results-title">How the fixes held up.</h2></div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/benchmark/leaderboard">Explore the results <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <p class="section-intro">We tested patches against SQL injection attacks and normal inputs. A fix has to stop the attack and keep the application working.</p>
    <div class="results-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Provider results, scroll horizontally on small screens" tabindex="0">
      <table class="results-table">
        <caption>Pilot 001 · blind run · 14 September 2026</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Provider / tool</th><th scope="col">Patches scored</th><th scope="col">Blocked all attacks</th><th scope="col">Preserved behaviour</th><th scope="col">Verified</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{rows.map(({ tool, version, tally: t }) => <tr>
          <th scope="row">{tool}<span>{version}</span></th>
          <td>{t.scored}</td><td>{t.holeShut}/{t.scored}</td><td>{t.behaviourHeld}/{t.scored}</td><td><span class="result-value">{t.verified}/{t.scored}</span></td>
        </tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-note"><p>Small pilot, not a general ranking. Only scored patches count; “no alert” cases are excluded. These are tested tools, not partners.</p><a href={`${ASSAY_SOURCE.repo}/tree/${ASSAY_SOURCE.commit}`}>Inspect the evidence ↗</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-section shell workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your workflow</p>
    <h2 id="workflow-title">Keep your fixer.<br /><span>Check its work.</span></h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Bring a patch from the tool you already use. Assay checks what changed.</p>
    <ol class="workflow-steps">
      <li><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Bring a patch</h3><p>Choose a SQL challenge. Give it to your AI tool, then bring back the fix.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Run the checks</h3><p>Check the scanner alert, unseen attacks, normal inputs and suppressed warnings.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Inspect the verdict</h3><p>See which checks passed, which failed and the evidence behind the result.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="workflow-status"><span class="status-dot"></span>{SCORING_LIVE ? 'Benchmark scoring is live.' : 'Hosted scoring is coming soon.'} Automated checks on your own pull requests are in development.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="landing-cta shell" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Start with one fix</p>
    <h2 id="cta-title">Put a patch to the test.</h2>
    <p>Four SQL injection challenges. Real checks. Evidence you can inspect.</p>
    <div class="cta-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/benchmark">Score a patch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><ContactButton /></div>
    {!SCORING_LIVE && <p class="availability">Explore the challenges now. Join the waitlist for scoring.</p>}
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
